# CRITICAL AI RULES - NEVER VIOLATE THESE

## 1. NEVER DELETE CODE WITHOUT EXPLICIT USER PERMISSION
- Do not delete files to "fix" OAuth issues or push failures
- Do not remove working features to resolve type errors
- Always ask before removing any file over 50 lines
- Git push failures are NOT solved by deleting code
- When you can't push, tell the user - don't delete files

## 2. TYPE SYSTEM RULES
- Types must be defined BEFORE implementation
- Use existing types from src/types/core.ts
- DO NOT create new Message/Chat types - use Message from @/types/core
- All new code must pass strict TypeScript checks
- No 'any' types except in migration code marked with // TODO: migrate
- When creating a "unified" solution, DELETE the old solutions in the SAME commit

## 3. DUPLICATE PREVENTION RULES
- Before creating a new type/hook/component, search for existing ones
- If creating a "unified" solution, you MUST delete old solutions immediately
- No more: "Create unified X" → old X still exists → now have both
- Pattern: "Replace X with unified X" → delete old X → only one X exists
- If you find duplicates, consolidate to ONE and delete the others

## 4. CONFIGURATION RULES
- NO hardcoded URLs - use environment variables
- NO hardcoded API keys - use env vars
- NO hardcoded model names - use constants from src/config/constants.ts
- All config in src/config/* files
- WebSocket URLs must come from WEBSOCKET_CONFIG
- Model names must come from GEMINI_MODELS

## 5. TESTING RULES
- Changes must not break existing tests
- New features require at least one test
- Run `pnpm type-check` before committing
- If tests fail, fix them - don't disable or delete tests

## 6. VOICE/WEBSOCKET RULES
- WebSocket URL: use WEBSOCKET_CONFIG.URL from @/config/constants
- Gemini Live API: use sendRealtimeInput() not session.send()
- Voice hooks: ONLY use useRealtimeVoice.ts (NOT useWebSocketVoice.ts)
- Model names: use GEMINI_MODELS constants from @/config/constants
- Voice model: MUST use model with `-native-audio-` for Live API support
- Current model: gemini-2.5-flash-native-audio-preview-09-2025
- Source of truth: .cursor/rules/gemini-voice-model-sot.md
- Before changing DEFAULT_VOICE: read source of truth documentation

## 7. COMMIT RULES
- No "comprehensive fixes" - be specific about what you fixed
- No "major refactors" without explicit approval
- Fixes should target one subsystem at a time
- Commit format: "fix: Specific thing in Specific file" not "fix: types"
- When consolidating duplicates, commit message must say what was deleted

## 8. FILE ORGANIZATION RULES
- Types: src/types/core.ts (canonical types only)
- Config: src/config/constants.ts (all constants)
- Voice/Multimodal: src/hooks/useLiveApi.ts (public API for components)
  - Internal: src/hooks/useRealtimeVoice.ts (WebSocket implementation - not directly imported)
- Chat API: app/api/chat/unified/route.ts (single route)
- NO local type definitions - import from @/types/core

## 9. MIGRATION RULES
- When migrating to new pattern, update ALL usages
- Don't leave half-migrated code
- If migration is incomplete, mark with // TODO: complete migration to [pattern]
- Delete deprecated code after migration is complete

## 10. ERROR HANDLING RULES
- TypeScript errors mean FIX THE TYPES, not disable strict mode
- Build failures mean FIX THE CODE, not relax the checks
- If you can't fix an error, ASK THE USER, don't workaround
- Never add @ts-ignore without a detailed comment explaining why

